WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.810
Open the kitchen drawer: two old
phones and a tangle of chargers.

2
00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:06.230
Nobody uses them.

3
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:07.710
Nobody throws them out.

4
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.410
They just sit there.

5
00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:11.130
Now zoom out.

6
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:17.410
Billions of phones are replaced, and in
2022 the world produced 62 million tonnes

7
00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:18.770
of e-waste.

8
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:23.350
So does one phone sitting in your
drawer really matter to the planet?

9
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.610
In this mission, you'll follow
a device through its life:

10
00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:30.050
made from mined materials, used, replaced,

11
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.630
then thrown away.

12
00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:36.070
You'll see why much of the impact happens
before you even switch a device on.

13
00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:41.030
And you'll discover how little of the
world's e-waste is documented as recycled.

14
00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:45.520
Your mission: explain why an old phone
in a drawer matters to the planet.
